<pipeline>
  <info>
    <name>trf_data_vault_link_sat_validity_generic_a</name>
    <name_sync_with_filename>Y</name_sync_with_filename>
    <description>Generic transformation: link validity satellite part a</description>
    <extended_description>This transformation processes a link validity satellite. These are necessary when the business key of a link is smaller then then all combined columns.
An example:
Suppose there's a link between an employer and an employee, but an employee can only work for 1 employer at a time.
The business key of the link is the hub_id of the employee in this case.
When the employee switches employer, the satellite with the old employer gets invalid, the satellite with the new employer gets inserted or gets valid again (if the employee worked for that employer before).

All sources for a link have a say in the validity status.
The sources get processed in the reversed order (compared to the order when processing the link), because the most important source has the last say then.

The steps are:

1:	Determine all the links with changed 'non business key'-columns.
2:	Close the currently valid satellite with the current load_dts.
3:	Insert an invalid satellite for the 'old' value.

When steps 1-3 have finished:

4:	Close all valid satellites with load_end_dts = 'current', update load_end_dts to current load_dts. 
5:	Insert a valid satellite for the 'new' value.
</extended_description>
    <pipeline_version>1.7</pipeline_version>
    <pipeline_type>Normal</pipeline_type>
    <pipeline_status>2</pipeline_status>
    <directory>/data_vault</directory>
    <parameters>
